<div class="wrap">
  <div class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">iPhone, iPad, and Mac</p>
    <h1>A private budget that lives in your iCloud.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Assign income to the month ahead, keep an eye on spending, and watch net worth over time. No ads, no bank login, and no account with us.</p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="btn primary" href="/guides/quick-start/">Read the quick start</a>
      <a class="btn secondary" href="/guides/">Browse guides</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="promises">
    <article class="card">
      <h2>Your iCloud, not our servers</h2>
      <p>Budgets stay in your private iCloud. We never receive your transactions, and there is nothing of yours for us to sell.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h2>Assign the month</h2>
      <p>Income waits in Ready to Assign until you give it a category. Anything still waiting stays visible.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h2>Offline, then it syncs</h2>
      <p>Add and edit with no connection. When you are back online, iCloud brings your devices back together.</p>
    </article>
  </div>

  <p class="section-label">First session</p>
  <div class="steps">
    <article class="card">
      <div class="num">1</div>
      <h3>Create a budget</h3>
      <p>Name it, pick a currency, and start from a category template or a blank plan.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <div class="num">2</div>
      <h3>Set account balances</h3>
      <p>Chequing and a credit card are already there at zero. Set today’s balance, and add any other accounts you spend from.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <div class="num">3</div>
      <h3>Assign income</h3>
      <p>New money lands in Ready to Assign. Move it into categories for the month.</p>
    </article>
  </div>

  <p class="section-label">What you can do</p>
  <div class="features">
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Categories and targets</h3>
      <p>Group spending, set a monthly or save-by date target, and see what is still available.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Credit cards</h3>
      <p>Spending on a card sets aside the payment in its own category.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Reports</h3>
      <p>Spending by category and a net-worth history, on the device that holds the data.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>More than one currency</h3>
      <p>Foreign accounts convert with public exchange rates. The budget’s home currency stays put.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Share a budget</h3>
      <p>Invite someone through iCloud. They see that budget, and we are not in the middle.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Receipts</h3>
      <p>Attach a photo or scan a receipt on device. The image stays with the transaction.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Backups</h3>
      <p>Export an archive you can restore later, plus a daily copy in your iCloud Drive.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Bring a plan with you</h3>
      <p>A guided import reads a CSV export of a register and a category plan.</p>
    </article>
  </div>

  <div class="price">
    <div>
      <strong>Free to download. Six months to decide.</strong>
      <p>After the trial, one annual subscription billed by Apple, with Family Sharing. Your country’s price is on the App Store page.</p>
    </div>
    <span class="pill">6-month trial</span>
  </div>
</div>
